# Project Walkthrough: Comparative Analysis of Global, Local, and Multiscale Quantum Kernels

We have designed, implemented, mathematically validated, and benchmarked a complete Quantum Machine Learning framework to evaluate **Global Fidelity**, **Local (Patch-wise Reduced Density Matrix)**, and **Multiscale** quantum kernel methods across four medical imaging benchmarks from **MedMNIST** (**PneumoniaMNIST**, **BreastMNIST**, **RetinaMNIST**, and **BloodMNIST**).

---

## 1. What Was Accomplished

1. **Modular Architecture Built**:
   - **Classical Preprocessing**: Strictly train-fitted PCA (8 components) and MinMaxScaler to $[-\pi, \pi]$ preventing any test data leakage ([`src/data/preprocessor.py`](file:///d:/quantum/src/data/preprocessor.py)).
   - **Dataset Ingestion**: Automated MedMNIST caching, preprocessing, and stratified sampling ([`src/data/loader.py`](file:///d:/quantum/src/data/loader.py)).
   - **Vectorized Quantum Simulation**: Batch-optimized statevector and tensor contraction engine computing exact reduced density matrices (RDMs) and Gram matrices in milliseconds ([`src/quantum/circuits.py`](file:///d:/quantum/src/quantum/circuits.py), [`src/quantum/density_matrix.py`](file:///d:/quantum/src/quantum/density_matrix.py), [`src/quantum/kernels.py`](file:///d:/quantum/src/quantum/kernels.py)).
   - **Deep Metric Extraction**: Mathematical implementations of Effective Rank ($\exp(H(p))$), Centered Kernel Target Alignment (KTA), and Off-diagonal concentration statistics ($\mu_{\text{off}}, \sigma^2_{\text{off}}$) ([`src/metrics/`](file:///d:/quantum/src/metrics)).
   - **QSVM & Classical Baselines**: Cross-validated QSVM and classical SVM (RBF & Linear) on identical 8 PCA features ([`src/models/`](file:///d:/quantum/src/models)).
   - **Automated Experiment Engine**: Master CLI script for single-dataset runs, full benchmarks, $\alpha$-sweeps, and sample size scaling ([`run_experiments.py`](file:///d:/quantum/run_experiments.py)).
   - **Academic Research Paper**: Comprehensive scientific report with derivations, tables, and theoretical analyses ([`reports/research_paper.md`](file:///d:/quantum/reports/research_paper.md)).

2. **Automated Unit Tests**:
   - Executed 13 automated unit tests in `pytest`: 100% passed in 23.5s.
   - Verified kernel symmetry, positive semi-definiteness ($\lambda_{\min} \ge 0$), unit diagonals ($K_{ii} = 1.0$), RDM Hermiticity and unit trace, metric bounds, and data leakage prevention.

